$ jailops logs forward list
NAME   TYPE     TO                FACILITY   SOURCES
file   syslog   udp://127.0.0.1   local0     messages+apps of all jails
! jailops: the list of jailopsd.yaml (logging.forward) is in force

$ jailops logs forward add syslog --to tls://logs.example.com:6514 --facility local3 --jail web -l tier=front
log-sink/logs added (syslog tls://logs.example.com:6514)

$ jailops --dry-run logs forward add webhook --to https://hooks.example.com/jailops --token-file /usr/local/etc/jailops/hook.token --audit-only
dry-run: would add log sink
name: hooks
type: webhook
to: https://hooks.example.com/jailops
token_file: /usr/local/etc/jailops/hook.token
sources:
  no_jails: true
  audit: true

$ jailops logs forward add webhook --to https://hooks.example.com/jailops --token-file /usr/local/etc/jailops/hook.token --audit-only
log-sink/hooks added (webhook https://hooks.example.com/jailops)

$ jailops logs forward add syslog --to udp://192.0.2.10 --name lan
log-sink/lan added (syslog udp://192.0.2.10)
! warning: plain udp to 192.0.2.10:514 sends the logs in the clear; use tls://

$ jailops logs forward list
NAME    TYPE      TO                                  FACILITY   SOURCES
file    syslog    udp://127.0.0.1                     local0     messages+apps of all jails
logs    syslog    tls://logs.example.com:6514         local3     messages+apps of jails=web tier=front
hooks   webhook   https://hooks.example.com/jailops   -          audit
lan     syslog    udp://192.0.2.10                    local0     messages+apps of all jails
! jailops: the list stored through the API is in force (generation 3); 'logs forward reset' returns to jailopsd.yaml

$ jailops logs forward edit logs --facility local5 --file messages --file auth.log
log-sink/logs updated

$ jailops logs forward list -o yaml
- name: file
  type: syslog
  to: udp://127.0.0.1
- name: logs
  type: syslog
  to: tls://logs.example.com:6514
  facility: local5
  sources:
    jails:
      - web
    labels:
      tier: front
    files:
      - messages
      - auth.log
- name: hooks
  type: webhook
  to: https://hooks.example.com/jailops
  token_file: /usr/local/etc/jailops/hook.token
  sources:
    no_jails: true
    audit: true
- name: lan
  type: syslog
  to: udp://192.0.2.10

$ jailops logs forward status
NAME    STATE     TO                                  FILES   SENT   QUEUED   DROPPED               LAST SENT   FAILING SINCE   LAST ERROR
file    idle      udp://127.0.0.1                     0       0      0        0                     -           -               -
logs    ok        tls://logs.example.com:6514         2       120    0        0                     3h          -               -
hooks   failing   https://hooks.example.com/jailops   0       0      40       7 (+2.0 KiB unread)   -           3h              HTTP 503: busy
lan     idle      udp://192.0.2.10                    0       0      0        0                     -           -               -
! warning: lan: plain udp to 192.0.2.10:514 sends the logs in the clear; use tls://

$ jailops logs forward test logs
sent to logs in 3 ms: jailops log forwarding test 000001 from fake-host

